WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.430
I asked a chatbot for 6B’s

2
00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.410
timetable for tomorrow.

3
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.290
It wrote a lovely, confident

4
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.250
timetable, all made up!

5
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.610
It never looked at our real one.

6
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:14.170
So what would make it actually check?

7
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.770
Today: from a chatbot that

8
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.070
talks to an agent that acts.

9
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.490
A chatbot is a language model

10
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.230
that writes text back to you.

11
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.990
It predicts likely words, one

12
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.210
small piece at a time.

13
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.320
On its own, it can’t look

14
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.780
anything up or do anything.

15
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.340
An agent is a language model

16
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.860
in a loop with tools.

17
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.580
Tools are small programs it can

18
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.120
ask for: a timetable, the weather,

19
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.240
a calculator, a reminder.

20
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.800
The model writes a request for a

21
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.760
tool, and the app runs it.

22
00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.050
So, an AI agent is a language model

23
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.490
that uses tools to get a job done.

24
00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.960
It reads your request, plans, calls

25
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.580
a tool and reads the result.

26
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.540
Then it answers, or calls

27
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.560
another tool first.

28
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.550
Here’s a real one, from Darsi Tiny, a

29
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.170
small model that runs on your phone.

30
00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.170
I asked: what’s the

31
00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:15.750
weather in Kafi tomorrow?

32
00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.040
It planned to check the weather,

33
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.880
then wrote this call: the tool’s

34
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.640
name, the place and the day.

35
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.090
The app runs the tool and adds the

36
00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.630
result: sunny, a high of thirty-five,

37
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.210
a ten percent chance of rain.

38
00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:35.070
Darsi Tiny reads that and answers.

39
00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:39.110
Request, plan, call, result,

40
00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.390
answer: that’s the loop.

41
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:43.190
Quick check!

42
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.800
In an agent, who actually

43
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.360
runs the weather tool?

44
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:49.960
The app.

45
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.000
The model only writes text: a

46
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.880
plan, a call, an answer.

47
00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.540
The app runs the tool and

48
00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.520
hands back the result.

49
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.810
That matters: the app is where we can

50
00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.690
check things before they happen.

51
00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.710
You may already meet agents.

52
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.700
A phone assistant that sets an alarm.

53
00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.930
A map that finds a route,

54
00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.610
then checks the traffic.

55
00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.510
At school, an agent could read the

56
00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.750
timetable, set reminders or find library

57
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:20.190
books.

58
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.380
In the app, pick a request and press One

59
00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:28.080
step: the plan, the call, the result and

60
00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.360
the answer appear in turn.

61
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.760
Try the trip from Kafi to

62
00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.700
Dala, with two tools.

63
00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:37.150
And open What Darsi Tiny

64
00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.690
sees: it’s all one text.

65
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:41.500
Your turn.

66
00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.410
My chatbot made up a timetable.

67
00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.370
What would turn it into an

68
00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.450
agent that checks?

69
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.860
A timetable tool it can call.

70
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.000
Remember: a chatbot talks, while

71
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.140
an agent uses tools to act.

72
00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.370
The loop is request, plan,

73
00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:02.210
call, result, answer.

74
00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.410
The model writes, and the

75
00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:05.770
app runs the tools.

76
00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.610
Try it in class tomorrow:

77
00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.090
play Human agent.

78
00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.920
One pupil is the model and

79
00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.520
writes a plan and a tool call.

80
00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.110
Another is the timetable tool

81
00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.650
and answers from the board.

82
00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.260
The class checks: did the

83
00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.740
answer come from the result?
